{
 "html": "<b>Verdict (FourCastNet 3): close.</b> FCN3 is a probabilistic model. Its 4-member mean scores 299 vs IFS HRES 296 on day-5 z500 (+1%) and 1.74 vs 1.91 K on T850 (-9%) on the same 6 starts, beating HRES on 7 of 9 variable\u2013lead pairs. A single member (394) matches an IFS ensemble member (WB2 397).",
 "stamp_html": "<h2>Run details</h2>Model: NVIDIA FourCastNet 3 via Earth2Studio 0.19.0, NVIDIA weights (commercially usable).<br>Initial conditions and truth: ERA5 (ARCO public zarr). IFS HRES: WeatherBench2 public zarr.<br>12 starts in 2020 (WB2's test year, outside training), 00 UTC, leads 1/3/5 days, latitude-weighted RMSE at 0.25\u00b0.<br>Machine: qBraid gpu-a100-sxm (NVIDIA A100 80GB PCIe), 2.64 s per 6 h step, model load 54.1 s.<br>Ensemble: 4 members (seeds 1000+) on 6 of the starts.<br>Wall time 21 min \u00b7 compute cost \u2248 $1.80 \u00b7 2026-10-01.",
 "tour": [
  {
   "lon": -40,
   "lat": 15,
   "dist": 4.8,
   "lead": 0,
   "html": "<b>One GPU, five days of weather.</b> NVIDIA FourCastNet 3 steps the whole atmosphere 6 h at a time from the ERA5 state of 24 Aug 2020, 00 UTC. Moisture, winds at 850 hPa and 500 hPa height contours are all model output.",
   "ov": "tcwv",
   "mode": "fc",
   "hold": 5000
  },
  {
   "lon": -74,
   "lat": 19,
   "dist": 2.3,
   "lead": 0,
   "html": "<b>Hurricane Laura</b> starts as a tropical storm near Hispaniola. Its moisture core is the bright plume, and the particles trace the model's own winds.",
   "ov": "tcwv",
   "mode": "fc",
   "hold": 4000
  },
  {
   "lon": -86,
   "lat": 24,
   "dist": 2.2,
   "lead": 0,
   "html": "Play forward. <b>Cyan</b> is the forecast track, <b>red</b> is ERA5. For two days they agree to within about 170 km.",
   "ov": "msl",
   "mode": "fc",
   "play_to": 48,
   "hold": 7000
  },
  {
   "lon": -90,
   "lat": 26,
   "dist": 2.0,
   "lead": 72,
   "html": "At +72 h the forecast centre is <b>185 km</b> from ERA5's, with 983 vs 978 hPa. The real Laura recurves north into Louisiana; FourCastNet 3 follows it. Drag the divider to compare.",
   "ov": "msl",
   "mode": "swipe",
   "hold": 7500
  },
  {
   "lon": 127,
   "lat": 31,
   "dist": 2.5,
   "lead": 72,
   "html": "<b>Typhoon Bavi</b> in the Yellow Sea, half a world away, comes out of the same forward pass. Here the forecast centre is 153 km from ERA5's at +72 h.",
   "ov": "tcwv",
   "mode": "fc",
   "hold": 5500
  },
  {
   "lon": 20,
   "lat": -45,
   "dist": 3.4,
   "lead": 120,
   "html": "Day-5 error in 2 m temperature. Most of the error sits in the Southern Ocean storm track and over the continents, where small-scale weather has been smoothed out.",
   "ov": "t2m",
   "mode": "err",
   "hold": 6500
  },
